# R-3.3 process log view in the real Neovim UI.
#
# Stage a hunk, then open the process log with the profile's binding (`$` in
# standard, `g $` in vim). The staging command must be recorded as a `git
# apply` entry, and `q` must return to the status view behind it.
#
# XFAIL: the Neovim client has no main-placement view manager (R-NV-2). Every
# pushed descriptor goes through `menu.lua`, which opens a one-line float, and
# the process log's `view/render` is then dropped by `init.lua` because its
# view id is not the status view's. The view therefore never shows text, so
# this scenario fails at `wait screen contains "Process log"` until R-NV-2
# lands; remove this tag only when the real client can display the view.
xfail: R-NV-2
fixture: modified-two-files
---
wait
keys: j j j j j j j j j j Right Right Right Right
wait
expect cursor on "+line3 CHANGED"
keys: s
wait
expect screen contains "Staged changes (1)"
keys standard: $
keys vim: g $
wait screen contains "Process log"
expect screen contains "git apply"
snapshot: process-log
keys: q
wait
expect screen contains "Unstaged changes"
snapshot: back-to-status
